===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[follower]] of [[Sunnism]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[Sunni#Adjective|Sunni]] Islam.
#* {{quote-book|title=Masculinity and Femininity: The Taboo Dimension of National Cultures|page=205|books.google.com/books?isbn=0761910298|author=[[w:Geert Hofstede|Geert H. Hofstede]]|year=1998|passage=In Islam, '''Sunni''' is a more triumphant version of the faith than Shia, which stresses the importance of suffering, following the founder Ali, who was persecuted.}}
#* {{quote-book|title=CIA World Factbook 2010|year=2009|page=xxviii|books.google.com/books?isbn=1602397279|author=Central Intelligence Agency|passage='''Sunni''' has four schools of Islamic doctrine and law — Hanafi, Maliki, Shafi'i, and Hanbali — which uniquely interpret the Hadith, or recorded oral traditions of Muhammad.}}
#* {{quote-book|title=Routledge Companion to Military Conflict since 1945|page=129|books.google.com/books?isbn=0203014707|author=John Richard Thackrah - 2008|passage='''Sunni''' is the mainstream religion, based in Mecca, and is generally more moderate.}}

